  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is neutral or negative (sentiment ≤ 0.00) to counteract overconfidence.",
    "Reduce forecast magnitude by 5-10% if recent 7-day mean reversion is observed (true outcome < 3-day moving average of history).",
    "Increase forecast lag by 1-2 days if model shows early spike followed by overshoot (forecast > true outcome by >10% for 2+ consecutive days).",
    "Apply upward bias correction if sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0.00) and true outcome is consistently below forecast — model may be underestimating bullish momentum.",
    "Cap forecast at 10% above 30-day historical high if sentiment is positive and price is trending upward — avoid over-leveraging bullish expectations.",
    "Use sentiment as a volatility filter: if sentiment = 0.00, apply no adjustment; if sentiment > 0.00, apply +3% bias; if sentiment < 0.00, apply -5% bias."
